---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="About Phasora — reconfigurable silicon for the age of intelligence." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="pt-36 md:pt-44 pb-24">
			<section class="container-x">
				<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
					<span class="section-eyebrow">About</span>
					<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-6xl">
						We&rsquo;re here to make AI compute <span class="text-gradient-accent">programmable again</span>.
					</h1>
					<p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
						Phasora was founded in 2024 by a group of FPGA architects, ML compiler engineers,
						and systems researchers. We build reconfigurable compute fabrics for teams that
						need lower latency, lower power, and tighter control over every cycle — from
						defense and aerospace to autonomy and frontier research.
					</p>

					<div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
						<p>
							The last decade has been about scaling models. The next will be about scaling
							<em class="text-white">specificity</em>: shaping the silicon to fit the model, not
							the other way around. Reconfigurable hardware — FPGAs today, custom ASICs
							tomorrow — gives us a path to do that without the multi-year tape-out latency
							of a traditional silicon company.
						</p>
						<p>
							We work end-to-end. Our compilers, runtimes, and toolchains let any PyTorch
							team target our hardware. Our research group co-designs operators and kernels
							with our hardware team so nothing gets lost in translation. And our deployment
							engineers make sure what ships to a customer rack today gets better, with OTA
							bitstream updates, in the months that follow.
						</p>
						<p>
							If any of that sounds like the kind of problem you want to spend the next five
							years on, we&rsquo;d love to hear from you.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
						<a href="/#projects" class="btn btn-primary">See current projects</a>
						<a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Get in touch</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
